==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[attonce]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|at}} + {{term|once}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ət ˈwʌns/}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|head=[[at]] [[once]]|-}}

# {{obsolete}} In [[one]] group; [[together]].
#* '''1590''', {{w|Edmund Spenser}}, ''The Faerie Queene'', III.4:
#*: Those two great champions did '''attonce''' pursew / The fearefull damzell with incessany payns [...].
# {{idiomatic}} [[at the same time|At the same time]]; [[simultaneously]].
#: ''Can you pat your head and rub your belly '''at once'''?''
#: ''He tried to eat four cookies '''at once.'''''
# {{idiomatic}} [[immediately|Immediately]]; [[now]]; [[right away]].
#: ''Tell the doctor to come '''at once'''. She is having a baby.''

